    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my 2018 civic is making this loud squealing noise whenever i step on the gas. i think it might be a belt issue? can u explain what the serpentine belt actually does and why a worn one would make that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The serpentine belt is a toothed belt that powers various engine components, such as the alternator, power steering pump, air conditioning compressor, and IDles the engine's fuel pump. A worn or slipping serpentine belt can cause a loud squealing or screeching noise when you accelerate or shift gears, as it can't maintain proper tension on these components. If the belt is worn, the uneven wear can cause the noise to intensify, especially when accelerating or idling, as the belt slips between pulleys, causing vibrations.",
